# React Codebase Navigation

## Package Structure Reference

When navigating React source code, use these key entry points:

### Core Packages
- **react**: [packages/react/src/ReactClient.js](../packages/react/src/ReactClient.js) - Public API exports
- **react-dom**: [packages/react-dom/src/client/ReactDOMClient.js](../packages/react-dom/src/client/ReactDOMClient.js) - DOM renderer entry
- **react-reconciler**: [packages/react-reconciler/src/ReactFiberReconciler.js](../packages/react-reconciler/src/ReactFiberReconciler.js) - Core reconciler
- **scheduler**: [packages/scheduler/src/Scheduler.js](../packages/scheduler/src/Scheduler.js) - Time slicing

### Analysis Documentation
Always link analysis back to:
- [Project Overview](mdc:analysis/overview.md) - High-level architecture
- [Analysis TODO](mdc:analysis/TODO.md) - Current focus areas

### Code Reference Standards
1. **Always include line numbers** in file references
2. **Link to specific functions** rather than entire files when possible
3. **Reference related analysis** documents for context
4. **Update TODO list** when completing analysis sections

